:232,"stem":233,"icon":234},"CRI Format","\u002Fplatform\u002Freference\u002Fcri-format","04.platform\u002F12.reference\u002F01.cri-format","i-lucide-link",{"title":236,"path":237,"stem":238,"icon":239},"Grind Jobs","\u002Fplatform\u002Freference\u002Fgrind-jobs","04.platform\u002F12.reference\u002F02.grind-jobs","i-lucide-workflow",{"title":241,"path":242,"stem":243,"icon":178},"Project Publishing Design","\u002Fplatform\u002Freference\u002Fproject-publishing-design","04.platform\u002F12.reference\u002F03.project-publishing-design",{"title":245,"path":246,"stem":247,"icon":33},"Sign-In Design","\u002Fplatform\u002Freference\u002Fsign-in-design","04.platform\u002F12.reference\u002F04.sign-in-design",{"title":249,"path":250,"stem":251,"icon":252},"Development Server","\u002Fplatform\u002Fdevelopment-server","04.platform\u002F13.development-server","i-lucide-server-cog",{"title":254,"path":255,"stem":256,"icon":257},"Supply Chain Security","\u002Fplatform\u002Fsupply-chain-security","04.platform\u002F14.supply-chain-security","i-lucide-package-check",{"title":259,"path":260,"stem":261,"icon":262},"Enterprise License","\u002Fplatform\u002Fenterprise-license","04.platform\u002F15.enterprise-license","i-lucide-badge-check",{"id":264,"title":15,"body":265,"description":529,"extension":530,"links":531,"meta":532,"navigation":533,"path":16,"seo":534,"stem":17,"__hash__":535},"docs\u002F01.getting-started\u002F02.quick-start.md",{"type":266,"value":267,"toc":525},"minimark",[268,272,495,500,503,521],[269,270,271],"p",{},"Try Kinotic Cloud, where Kinotic runs for you, free while it is in beta, or run Kinotic on your own machine.",[273,274,276,284],"tabs",{"sync":275},"kinotic-install",[277,278,281],"tabs-item",{"icon":279,"label":280},"i-lucide-cloud","Cloud",[282,283],"cloud-beta",{},[277,285,288,291,296,333,466],{"icon":286,"label":287},"i-lucide-laptop","Local",[269,289,290],{},"The local install runs the whole of Kinotic OS in Docker on your machine: its servers, the portal, the\nGit server that holds your projects' repositories, and the storage your apps' data and UIs live in.\nNothing leaves your machine except the downloads.",[292,293,295],"h4",{"id":294},"prerequisites","Prerequisites",[297,298,299,307,313,324,330],"ul",{},[300,301,302,306],"li",{},[303,304,305],"strong",{},"Docker"," with Compose, running, with at least 12 GB of memory available to it",[300,308,309,312],{},[303,310,311],{},"Node.js"," 18 or later, which the Kinotic CLI runs on",[300,314,315,318,319,323],{},[303,316,317],{},"macOS on Apple silicon, or Linux with KVM"," (",[320,321,322],"code",{},"\u002Fdev\u002Fkvm","), where your apps' deployments run as micro VMs",[300,325,326,329],{},[303,327,328],{},"Claude Code, Codex or Grok Build",", which builds your app with the Kinotic plugin",[300,331,332],{},"An internet connection for the first start, which downloads Kinotic, and for each new project, whose starting code comes from GitHub",[334,335,337,341,373,399,406,410,418,422,435,438,455,463],"steps",{"level":336},"4",[292,338,340],{"id":339},"install-and-launch-kinotic","Install and launch Kinotic",[342,343,348],"pre",{"className":344,"code":345,"language":346,"meta":347,"style":347},"language-bash shiki shiki-themes material-theme-lighter material-theme material-theme-palenight","curl -fsSL https:\u002F\u002Fkinotic.ai\u002Finstall | sh\n","bash","",[320,349,350],{"__ignoreMap":347},[351,352,355,359,363,366,370],"span",{"class":353,"line":354},"line",1,[351,356,358],{"class":357},"sBMFI","curl",[351,360,362],{"class":361},"sfazB"," -fsSL",[351,364,365],{"class":361}," https:\u002F\u002Fkinotic.ai\u002Finstall",[351,367,369],{"class":368},"sMK4o"," |",[351,371,372],{"class":357}," sh\n",[269,374,375,376,383,384,387,388,391,392,395,396,398],{},"This installs ",[377,378,382],"a",{"href":379,"rel":380},"https:\u002F\u002Fbun.sh",[381],"nofollow","Bun"," if you don't have it, installs the Kinotic CLI, adds Bun's bin\nfolder to your ",[320,385,386],{},"PATH"," in your shell's profile if it isn't there yet, and runs ",[320,389,390],{},"kinotic local up",", which\nstarts Kinotic and the node your projects deploy to. The first start downloads everything and prepares\nthe database, which takes a few minutes; the command returns once Kinotic is ready. Open a new terminal\nto use ",[320,393,394],{},"kinotic"," there. With the CLI already installed, ",[320,397,390],{}," alone starts it.",[269,400,401,402,405],{},"To update the CLI, run ",[320,403,404],{},"kinotic local down",", then the same line again.",[292,407,409],{"id":408},"create-your-organization","Create your organization",[269,411,412,413,417],{},"Open ",[377,414,415],{"href":415,"rel":416},"http:\u002F\u002Flocalhost:9090\u002Fsignup",[381],", enter your email, then your name,\nyour organization's name and a password. A local install sends no email, so the page goes straight on, and\nyou are signed in to your new organization.",[292,419,421],{"id":420},"follow-the-quickstart-in-the-portal","Follow the Quickstart in the portal",[269,423,412,424,426,427,430,431,434],{},[303,425,5],{}," in the portal's sidebar and choose the AI you use: Claude (Claude Code), ChatGPT\n(Codex) or Grok (Grok Build). The page gives you one message to copy and paste into a new session of\nthat coding agent. The message has the agent install the Kinotic plugin, add your local Kinotic as\nthe ",[320,428,429],{},"kinotic-local"," MCP server, tell you how to sign in, and ask what you want to build. The page\nalso lists the same setup under ",[303,432,433],{},"Prefer to set it up yourself?",", for doing it by hand.",[269,436,437],{},"Sign in as the agent tells you, and approve the consent screen that opens in your browser. Then say\nwhat you want to build: the agent creates the application and its project, writes the entities,\nservices and UIs, and pushes to the project's repository; every push deploys. The Quickstart checks\noff the sign-in, the project and its first deployment as they happen.",[269,439,440,441,443,444,447,448,450,451,454],{},"For local use, the agent connects to your Kinotic through ",[320,442,429],{},". In Claude Code's ",[320,445,446],{},"\u002Fmcp","\nlist, authenticate ",[320,449,429],{},". Don't worry about ",[320,452,453],{},"plugin:kinotic:kinotic-os"," in the same list:\nthe Kinotic plugin adds it for use with Kinotic Cloud, and local use doesn't need it.",[342,456,461],{"className":457,"code":459,"language":460,"meta":347},[458],"language-text","User MCPs\n❯ ⚠ kinotic-local                needs authentication    ← for local use: authenticate it\n\nBuilt-in MCPs\n  ⚠ plugin:kinotic:kinotic-os    needs authentication    ← for Kinotic Cloud: not needed locally\n","text",[320,462,459],{"__ignoreMap":347},[269,464,465],{},"If you also work on Kinotic Cloud, authenticate both: the agent works on each project through the\nserver that holds it, and asks which one to create a new app on.",[269,467,468,470,471,473,474,477,478,481,482,485,486,490,491,494],{},[320,469,404],{}," stops Kinotic and the apps it deployed, and keeps your data for the next ",[320,472,390],{},";\n",[320,475,476],{},"kinotic local down --delete-data"," deletes it. ",[320,479,480],{},"kinotic local status"," and ",[320,483,484],{},"kinotic local logs"," show what\nit is doing, and the ",[377,487,489],{"href":488},"\u002Fapps\u002Fcli-reference#kinotic-local","CLI reference"," covers each command.\n",[377,492,493],{"href":213},"Developing Kinotic"," covers how to work on Kinotic itself.",[496,497,499],"h2",{"id":498},"whats-next","What's Next?",[269,501,502],{},"Once your first app is deployed, explore the rest of the documentation:",[297,504,505,511,516],{},[300,506,507,510],{},[377,508,509],{"href":52},"Application Structure"," -- Understand how organizations, applications, projects, and artifacts are organized.",[300,512,513,515],{},[377,514,63],{"href":69}," -- Learn how to publish and consume services across your application.",[300,517,518,520],{},[377,519,88],{"href":94}," -- Dive deeper into entity definitions, relationships, and querying.",[522,523,524],"style",{},"html pre.shiki code .sBMFI, html code.shiki .sBMFI{--shiki-light:#E2931D;--shiki-default:#FFCB6B;--shiki-dark:#FFCB6B}html pre.shiki code .sfazB, html code.shiki .sfazB{--shiki-light:#91B859;--shiki-default:#C3E88D;--shiki-dark:#C3E88D}html pre.shiki code .sMK4o, html code.shiki .sMK4o{--shiki-light:#39ADB5;--shiki-default:#89DDFF;--shiki-dark:#89DDFF}html .light .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-light);background: var(--shiki-light-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-light-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-light-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-light-text-decoration);}html.light .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-light);background: var(--shiki-light-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-light-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-light-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-light-text-decoration);}html .default .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-default-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-default-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-default-text-decoration);}html .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-default-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-default-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-default-text-decoration);}html .dark .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-dark);background: var(--shiki-dark-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-dark-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-dark-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-dark-text-decoration);}html.dark .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-dark);background: var(--shiki-dark-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-dark-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-dark-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-dark-text-decoration);}",{"title":347,"searchDepth":526,"depth":526,"links":527},2,[528],{"id":498,"depth":526,"text":499},"Try Kinotic Cloud or run Kinotic on your own machine, create your organization, and build your first app with Claude Code, Codex or Grok Build.","md",null,{},true,{"title":15,"description":529},"GkvldfeYwK5X2e-41LCzLAIe_60sEoqwUn0Gc07vL8A",[537,539],{"title":11,"path":12,"stem":13,"description":538,"children":-1},"Learn what Kinotic is, why it exists, and how it helps developers and AI agents build enterprise-grade applications at scale.",{"title":26,"path":27,"stem":28,"description":540,"icon":21,"children":-1},"Set up a Kinotic organization -- its members, how they sign in, and the Apps it builds.",1795742984365]